diff --git a/apps/ios/EXPORTABLE_DOWNLOADS.md b/apps/ios/EXPORTABLE_DOWNLOADS.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1af56df
--- /dev/null
+++ b/apps/ios/EXPORTABLE_DOWNLOADS.md
@@ -0,0 +1,54 @@
+# Exportable offline downloads
+
+This branch makes iOS offline downloads visible and shareable without loading large
+media files into memory.
+
+## Behaviour
+
+- New files are stored under `Documents/Downloads`, which is exposed to the Files app
+  by `UIFileSharingEnabled` and `LSSupportsOpeningDocumentsInPlace`.
+- On first launch, an in-place app update moves the former
+  `Application Support/Downloads` directory to the new location. The move is normally
+  metadata-only on the same APFS volume, so it does not duplicate multi-gigabyte files.
+- A completed row offers **Share / Save to Files** by leading swipe or long press.
+- The share sheet receives a local file URL. A temporary hard link supplies a readable
+  title when possible; the video bytes are not copied.
+- New filenames include series, season/episode, title, and stream identifier while
+  being sanitized and limited to the filesystem component-size limit.
+- URLSession resume blobs remain private in Application Support because they may embed
+  authenticated provider URLs; only completed media is exposed through Files.
+
+## Existing App Store installation
+
+An app installed alongside the App Store build has a different signed application
+identity and cannot read the App Store app's container. Therefore:
+
+- if this patch ships as an update signed by the original developer, the migration can
+  expose downloads already present in that installation;
+- if it is installed as a separate fork, only downloads made by the fork are available.
+
+For a private side-by-side build, set a unique bundle identifier and display name in
+Xcode. Installing on a physical iPhone/iPad requires Xcode with a signing team, an
+Ad Hoc profile, or TestFlight/App Store Connect through an Apple Developer Program
+account.
+
+## Additional download fixes
+
+- background tasks carry a stable item/path context and restore in O(tasks + rows)
+  rather than scanning every database row for every task;
+- successful file finalization happens after the active queue slot is released,
+  removing a completion race that could leave the next item queued;
+- system cancellations without resume data are requeued cleanly instead of remaining
+  stuck as downloading;
+- explicit user cancellations cannot be mistaken for orphaned system cancellations;
+- a queued database row is atomically claimed before starting its network task;
+- Xtream stream URLs, which can contain credentials, are no longer written to logs;
+- downloaded paths and extensions are sanitized against path traversal and invalid
+  filenames.
+
+## Verification
+
+`DownloadStorageTests.swift` covers readable/safe episode paths, hostile path and
+extension input, Unicode filename length, and extension fallback. A signed iOS build
+and on-device test are still required for the Files provider, AirDrop, background
+URLSession relaunch, and migration flows.
